00:00:01.819 --> 00:00:04.400 align:start position:0%
once again the country is struggling to  understand acts of mass gun violence  after deadly attacks in two more  American cities and overnight the FBI  issued a new warning saying quote  violent extremists could become inspired  by these and previous high-profile  attacks to engage in similar acts of  violence the massacres in El Paso Texas  and Dayton Ohio happened in startling  proximity for a country already too  familiar with gun violence twenty nine  people were killed in the two shooting  rampages just 13 hours apart these are  some of the faces and names of those  killed the victims ranged in age from 15  to 86 the Justice Department says it is  treating the attack at the El Paso  Walmart as domestic terrorism at least  20 people were killed and 26 others were  hurt that toll makes it the eighth worst  mass shooting in modern American history  the 21 year old suspect is in custody  more than 1300 miles away in Dayton Ohio  at least nine people were killed in 27  wounded just after 1:00 a.m. Sunday  police officer shot and killed the  gunman less than 30 seconds after he  first opened fire  president Trump condemned the shootings  and said quote hate has no place in our  country
 

